      <!-- ================================================
           SECTION 1 — THE PROBLEM
           ================================================ -->
      <section class="as-section as-section--mid" id="s-problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
        <div class="as-section-inner">
          <header class="as-section-header">
            <span class="as-section-label label-red">Section 1</span>
            <h2 class="as-section-title" id="problem-title">
              The <span class="gradient-text--amber">Problem</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="as-section-desc">
              Shadow DOM is exceptional at style isolation — so exceptional that styles defined
              inside a component cannot reach slotted content. That content lives in the
              <strong>light DOM</strong>, outside the shadow boundary.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="as-problem-callout" role="alert">
            <span class="as-problem-callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128274;</span>
            <div class="as-problem-callout-body">
              <h3>The trip-planner team lost a full week to this</h3>
              <p>
                Upgrading to HELiX, their Drupal Twig templates put rich text content into
                component slots. The components looked perfect in Storybook. In production,
                headings had no color, links were bare blue, and paragraphs used browser defaults.
                Shadow DOM's encapsulation was working exactly as designed — and exactly as a blocker.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="as-grid-2">
            <div>
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); color: var(--text-primary);">
                Why styles don't reach slotted content
              </h3>
              <ul class="as-feature-list">
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-red);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>Shadow boundary blocks cascade.</strong> CSS defined in a shadow root
                    cannot style nodes distributed into a slot — they remain in the host's light DOM.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-red);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong><code>::slotted()</code> only covers one level.</strong> It styles direct slotted
                    children, not their descendants. A <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> inside a slotted
                    <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> is unreachable.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-red);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>Global CSS is too broad.</strong> Injecting styles at
                    <code>document</code> level pollutes every page element — not just component slots.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-red);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>Drupal Twig templates output light DOM.</strong> Every field value,
                    body text, and rich text area lands outside the shadow root, where component styles cannot touch it.
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="as-code-window" role="region" aria-label="Code example: broken styling">
                <div class="as-code-window-header">
                  <div class="as-code-dots" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span><span></span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="as-code-filename">hx-card.styles.ts — styles that WON'T reach slots</span>
                </div>
                <pre class="as-code"><code><span class="c-comment">/* This lives inside Shadow DOM */</span>
<span class="c-comment">/* It CANNOT style slotted content */</span>

<span class="c-tag">:host</span> {
  <span class="c-prop">display</span>: <span class="c-value">block</span>;
  <span class="c-prop">padding</span>: <span class="c-value">1.5rem</span>;
}

<span class="c-comment">/* Only direct slotted children */</span>
<span class="c-tag">::slotted(p)</span> {
  <span class="c-prop">color</span>: <span class="c-value">var(--hx-text-body)</span>; <span class="c-comment">/* OK */</span>
}

<span class="c-comment">/* BROKEN — descendants unreachable */</span>
<span class="c-tag">::slotted(div) p</span> {
  <span class="c-prop">color</span>: <span class="c-value">var(--hx-text-body)</span>; <span class="c-comment">/* ignored */</span>
}
<span class="c-tag">::slotted(article) h2</span> {
  <span class="c-prop">font-size</span>: <span class="c-value">1.5rem</span>; <span class="c-comment">/* ignored */</span>
}</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ================================================
           SECTION 2 — THE SOLUTION
           ================================================ -->
      <section class="as-section as-section--dark" id="s-solution" aria-labelledby="solution-title">
        <div class="as-section-inner">
          <header class="as-section-header">
            <span class="as-section-label label-cyan">Section 2</span>
            <h2 class="as-section-title" id="solution-title">
              The <span class="gradient-text">Solution</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="as-section-desc">
              <code class="as-inline-code">AdoptedStylesheetsController</code> injects a
              <code class="as-inline-code">CSSStyleSheet</code> directly into the
              <code class="as-inline-code">document.adoptedStyleSheets</code> array when your
              component connects — scoped, deduplicated, and automatically cleaned up when
              the last consumer disconnects.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="as-solution-callout">
            <span class="as-solution-callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</span>
            <div class="as-solution-callout-body">
              <h3>The default pattern — not optional</h3>
              <p>
                Adopted stylesheets are the <em>only</em> reliable way to style slotted content
                from inside a web component. This is not a workaround — it is the spec-compliant,
                browser-native solution that every HELiX consumer should reach for first.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="as-grid-2">
            <div>
              <div class="as-code-window" role="region" aria-label="Code example: AdoptedStylesheetsController usage">
                <div class="as-code-window-header">
                  <div class="as-code-dots" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span><span></span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="as-code-filename">hx-card.ts — 3 lines to fix everything</span>
                </div>
                <pre class="as-code"><code><span class="c-keyword">import</span> { <span class="c-type">LitElement</span>, html } <span class="c-keyword">from</span> <span class="c-string">'lit'</span>;
<span class="c-keyword">import</span> { customElement } <span class="c-keyword">from</span> <span class="c-string">'lit/decorators.js'</span>;
<span class="c-keyword">import</span> { <span class="c-type">AdoptedStylesheetsController</span> }
  <span class="c-keyword">from</span> <span class="c-string">'../controllers/adopted-stylesheets.js'</span>; <span class="c-comment">// 1</span>

<span class="c-tag">@customElement</span>(<span class="c-string">'hx-card'</span>)
<span class="c-keyword">export class</span> <span class="c-type">HxCard</span> <span class="c-keyword">extends</span> <span class="c-type">LitElement</span> {

  <span class="c-comment">// 2 — inject styles into document for slotted content</span>
  <span class="c-keyword">private</span> _slotStyles = <span class="c-keyword">new</span> <span class="c-type">AdoptedStylesheetsController</span>(
    <span class="c-call">this</span>,
    <span class="c-string">`
      hx-card p   { color: var(--hx-text-body);  }
      hx-card h2  { color: var(--hx-text-heading);}
      hx-card a   { color: var(--hx-color-primary);}
    `</span>           <span class="c-comment">// 3 — CSS targeting the host element in light DOM</span>
  );

  <span class="c-call">render</span>() {
    <span class="c-keyword">return</span> html<span class="c-string">`&lt;slot&gt;&lt;/slot&gt;`</span>;
  }
}</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); color: var(--text-primary);">
                What happens under the hood
              </h3>
              <ul class="as-feature-list">
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-green);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>hostConnected():</strong> Creates one <code>CSSStyleSheet</code>, calls
                    <code>replaceSync()</code>, adds it to <code>document.adoptedStyleSheets</code>.
                    Cached globally — second instance reuses the same sheet.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-green);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>Reference counting:</strong> Each consumer increments a counter keyed
                    by <code>cssText + rootId</code>. No stylesheet is removed while any consumer is live.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-green);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>hostDisconnected():</strong> Decrements the counter. Removes the stylesheet
                    from <code>adoptedStyleSheets</code> only when the count reaches zero.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="as-feature-item">
                  <span class="as-feature-icon" style="color: var(--wc-green);" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></span>
                  <span class="as-feature-text">
                    <strong>WeakMap root IDs:</strong> Each <code>Document</code> or
                    <code>ShadowRoot</code> gets a stable numeric ID so reference counts never
                    bleed across roots.
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
