              Performance <span class="gradient-text--amber">Characteristics</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="as-section-desc">
              The controller is engineered for enterprise scale. Every design choice
              prioritizes minimal overhead at hundreds-to-thousands of component instances.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="as-perf-grid" role="list" aria-label="Performance statistics">
            <div class="as-perf-stat" role="listitem">
              <div class="as-perf-stat-value gradient-text">1×</div>
              <div class="as-perf-stat-label">CSS parsed per unique string, regardless of instance count</div>
            </div>
            <div class="as-perf-stat" role="listitem">
              <div class="as-perf-stat-value" style="color: var(--wc-green);">0</div>
              <div class="as-perf-stat-label">Duplicate <code>CSSStyleSheet</code> objects created for identical CSS</div>
            </div>
            <div class="as-perf-stat" role="listitem">
              <div class="as-perf-stat-value" style="color: var(--wc-amber);">O(n)</div>
              <div class="as-perf-stat-label">Map lookup per connect/disconnect — constant time cache check</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="as-mechanic-grid" role="list" aria-label="Internal mechanics">
            <div class="as-mechanic-card" role="listitem">
              <h4 style="color: var(--wc-cyan);">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-database" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Static CSS Cache
              </h4>
              <p>
                <code>AdoptedStylesheetsController._cache</code> is a static
                <code>Map&lt;string, CSSStyleSheet&gt;</code> keyed by CSS text.
                The first component to use a given CSS string pays the parse cost.
                Every subsequent consumer — any component type, any instance count — gets
                the same object reference. Zero re-parsing.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="as-mechanic-card" role="listitem">
              <h4 style="color: var(--wc-accent);">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-calculator" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Reference Counting
              </h4>
              <p>
                <code>AdoptedStylesheetsController._refCounts</code> is a static
                <code>Map&lt;string, number&gt;</code>. The key is
                <code>cssText + "__" + rootId</code>. Incremented on connect,
                decremented on disconnect. The stylesheet is removed from
                <code>adoptedStyleSheets</code> only at count zero.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="as-mechanic-card" role="listitem">
              <h4 style="color: var(--wc-green);">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                WeakMap Root IDs
              </h4>
              <p>
                <code>AdoptedStylesheetsController._rootIds</code> is a static
                <code>WeakMap&lt;Document | ShadowRoot, number&gt;</code>.
                Each root gets a stable integer ID on first access. This prevents
                reference counts from bleeding between the document and shadow roots,
                or between different shadow roots.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="as-mechanic-card" role="listitem">
              <h4 style="color: var(--wc-amber);">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-shield" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Safe Deduplication Check
              </h4>
              <p>
                Before appending a sheet, the controller checks
                <code>root.adoptedStyleSheets.includes(sheet)</code>.
                If another instance already added the same sheet to the same root,
                it is not added again. This handles edge cases where multiple
                components of the same type connect simultaneously.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

